<title>LEBANON: Arab Bank publishes 1996 results. [CORRECTED 09:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Arab Bank publishes 1996 results. [CORRECTED 09:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arab Bank reported a nine percent rise in customer deposits, a 12.8 percent rise in assets and a 28.2 percent rise in loans and credits in 1996, according to annual results published in newspapers.</p>
<p>The balance sheet did not include net profits but according to Bankdata Financial Services, the bank's net profits, listed in the table below, fell by 20.9 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>Arab Bank issued the following results (in billions of Lebanese pounds. Rankings according to Bankdata Financial Services).</p>
<p>			1996    (rank)	   1995    (rank)</p>
<p>Net profits	   15.315   9	     18.516     8</p>
<p>(Corrects to 15.315 and 18.516 from 15,315 and 18,516 respectively.)</p>
<p>Assets		1,574.84   9	     1,395.32   9</p>
<p>Deposits	    1,408.28   9	     1,290.84   9</p>
<p>Loans</p>
<p>&amp; credits	   389.541    9	     303.952    9</p>
<p>(Corrects to 389.541 and 303.952 from 389,541 and 303,952 respectively.)</p>
<p>Arab Bank has 10 branches in Lebanon and it employs 558 people, according to the almanac of the Lebanese Banks Association.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,552 Lebanese pounds at 31/12/96)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 345723 345740 602057</p>
